k_uuid":"911248a7-b837-4b7b-9442-fab861b578f1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7b23-aad2-874a-4b32"},{"link_uuid":"34a43ff8-9400-4c22-9b77-5f5c39061a5f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2b03-d0d7-715a-44f7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:217-254` and generated `docs/mcp-reference.md:54` advertise plan-review P1-P9 while production executes P1-P11 (`plan_review/registry.py:118`, `det_floor.py:1`, `workflow_ops.py:13`). Code-review lifecycle comments across review-kernel, prompting, workflow, and review-workflow modules also contradict the shipped four-pass gate.\n\n## Approach\n\nCorrect the existing canonical tool descriptions and source-local ownership comments, then regenerate the current MCP reference with the existing generator. Do not introduce a second executable review-policy registry.\n\n## Scope\n\n- MCP LLM tool descriptions and affected review/code-review source comments\n- `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`, generated MCP reference, and its tests\n\n## Testing\n\nRegenerate the reference, run its generator test, and assert the canonical descriptions name P1-P11 and the current four-pass lifecycle.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Canonical MCP tool descriptions advertise P1-P11 exactly as implemented. Verified: `_mcp_llm.py`'s `review_plan` docstring corrected P1-P9 -> P1-P11.\n- [x] Canonical code-review comments describe the shipped four-pass execution rather than future, legacy, or single-pass states. Verified: 3 stale \"future code-review\" comments fixed in `review_kernel/__init__.py`, `review_kernel/discovery.py`, `prompting/prompts.py`.\n- [x] `docs/mcp-reference.md` is regenerated from the corrected source descriptions. Verified: regenerated via `python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_gen_mcp_reference.py` and focused documentation checks pass without adding a new registry. Verified: `test_gen_mcp_reference.py` + new `tests/unit/test_review_lifecycle_docs.py` (5 tests) -- 19 passed. No new registry added. Committed 68e5ca8ee7af, pushed as Gerrit change 2542, merged to main as `8c93586cfe1a`.\n\nFollow-up: a post-merge `review-plan` re-check (evaluated against landed `origin/main`) found two additional canonical JSON schema description fields still advertising the retired P1-P9 count -- `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_precheck_output.schema.json` and `plan_review_verdict.schema.json` -- missed by the original grep sweep. Fixed both to P1-P11, added 2 held-out regression tests (`test_plan_review_precheck_schema_names_p1_p11_floor`, `test_plan_review_verdict_schema_names_p1_p11_floor`) confirmed RED-then-GREEN, confirmed `det_advisory.py`/`det_lint.py`'s frozen historical \"P1-P9\" seam-boundary comments were correctly left untouched (pinned by the pre-existing `test_det_floor_seam_boundary_comments_keep_p1_p9_verbatim`). Committed `7e77bbb26e18`, pushed as Gerrit change 2554 (`LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`), merged to main as `8047cafb4f60`. `rebar review-plan` re-run: PASS.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"correct canonical MCP tool descriptions"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/__init__.py","reason":"correct review lifecycle ownership comment"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/discovery.py","reason":"correct review lifecycle comment"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py","reason":"correct canonical four-pass prose"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"correct workflow lifecycle comment"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/review_workflows.py","reason":"correct code-review execution comment"},{"path":"scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","reason":"regenerate current reference from canonical descriptions"},{"path":"docs/mcp-reference.md","reason":"generated MCP contract reference"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_mcp_reference.py","reason":"verify reference generation"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_precheck_output.schema.json","reason":"follow-up: correct stale P1-P9 floor reference to P1-P11 in schema description"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_verdict.schema.json","reason":"follow-up: correct stale P1-P9 floor reference to P1-P11 in schema description"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_lifecycle_docs.py","reason":"follow-up: add regression tests pinning P1-P11 floor in both schema descriptions"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"],["relates_to","2b03-d0d7-715a-44f7"],["relates_to","7b23-aad2-874a-4b32"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"b8c0447a-9ff0-47b1-8408-95c32b2226d2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["janitor","documentation","mcp","rp21"],"ticket_id":"ecb4-ceda-e276-4efb","ticket_type":"task","title":"Correct canonical review and gate descriptions and regenerate MCP reference","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f1ece06d-1eb0-4022-824a-19c3ad8844eb","ede8e0c7-731f-4cdf-96da-205e645791a4","95dfe9e3-ae36-40fc-b064-28498158b150","911248a7-b837-4b7b-9442-fab861b578f1","454cee34-65b5-4cb1-bff2-b9008ebdf7f0","34a43ff8-9400-4c22-9b77-5f5c39061a5f","65311428-5072-4ced-ba75-c36cb8ff373f","a332f486-5b41-402b-ba69-a39fe20778a2","e7635638-a1ce-46a0-b466-b32a832e7cf0","bf6b8192-f3b5-4e53-b207-27b5d7f9df5c","772b39f3-9b29-4485-86cc-cf54fd743c87","b8c0447a-9ff0-47b1-8408-95c32b2226d2","9f3f2ac5-3e4e-4a03-820a-b78523cb71b3"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788411712375310001,"uuid":"e9e35433-db3b-4fc2-a026-c5e1146f5483"}